course: dictionary
lesson: 14979
title: Making amends
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Sometimes you break something or hurt someone. Reparation is doing or paying something to make up for that wrong or damage. «Sam kicked a ball through the window, so he paid to have it mended.» Paying for the new glass is reparation, because it puts right what he broke.
explain: Reparation can also mean saying sorry and fixing things. «Mia made a mess in the hall, so she tidied it up and helped clean the floor.» Her clean-up is reparation. Ask yourself: what was the wrong, and what is being done to put it right?
explain: The word is often used in phrases: «make reparation», «pay reparations», and «reparation for». Reparations is the plural, and it usually means money. After a war, a country may have to pay reparations to the people it harmed.
fact: Reparation means doing or paying something to make up for a wrong or damage you caused.
fact: Reparations is the plural, and it often means money paid after a war or a wrong.
fact: In church, making reparation means making amends after confession.
fact: In school, restorative approaches ask pupils to make reparation to people they have hurt.
fact: Useful phrases: «make reparation», «pay reparations», «reparation for».
exercise: «Mia tidied up the mess she had made in the hall.» What is this an example of? | *Reparation | Winning a prize | Forgetting about it
exercise: What does «reparations» usually mean after a war? | A party to celebrate the peace | A map of the battlefield | *Money a country pays to make up for harm | A new army
exercise: Which word is the plural form of reparation? | repaid | *reparations | repair | repaired
test: «Tom broke his neighbour's fence, so he paid to fix it.» What did Tom make? | *Reparation | A promise to forget it | A new friend
test: In church, what does making reparation for sin mean? | Singing a hymn | *Making amends after confession | Going on holiday
exam: Which sentence shows reparation? | «She went to bed early.» | *«He paid for the window he broke.» | «He was given a prize for his drawing.»
